<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  German. Shares its wording with the iOS catalogue verbatim, for the same
  reason the English ones do: one product must not call a status "Am Schauen"
  on one phone and something else on the other.

  Two decisions worth knowing about, both in docs/LOCALISATION.md:

  "Benachrichtigungen" rather than Apple's "Mitteilungen", on both platforms.
  The house terms differ, and this project's rule is that the copy is shared;
  the Android word is the one a reader understands either way.

  The formal "Sie" is not used. The English copy speaks plainly and directly
  ("Know what you've watched"), and "du" keeps that; "Sie" would make the same
  sentences sound like a bank's.
-->
